 "notes": [
  "Variants are produced in the SAME simulator state: at every RoboTwin save step (every 15 physics steps) the head camera is rendered clean, then once per variant after swapping only render-side state (light colours, ambient light, wall/table-top render materials), then clean again; no physics step happens in between.",
  "Textures come from RoboTwin's assets/background_texture/unseen (the 'seen' split used by demo_randomized is not downloaded in this checkout); IDs were hand-picked for visible contrast. Light colours use RoboTwin's random_light formula U(0,1)^3 with fixed seeds (see variants.py).",
  "crazy_random_light normally re-draws colours every frame; here each variant keeps one draw for the whole episode so scrubbing time does not flicker.",
  "Head camera uses RoboTwin's Large_D435 profile (640x480, fovy 37 deg, same pose as the default 320x240 D435).",
  "Denoiser: OptiX (sapien's bundled OIDN 2.0.1 reports 'unsupported device type: CUDA' on H20)."
 ],
